Source tag: glibc-2.39
Translated source and modifications: https://github.com/acneism/lua-libm

The changes replace C unions with math.Float64bits, encode lookup tables as
read-only hexadecimal uint64 arrays with typed rows, share repeated polynomial
and reduction operations, spell out the FMA contractions selected by GCC's
final assembly, and make NaN selection explicit. A Go generator checks the
upstream SHA-256 manifest before reproducing the table source.
Floating-point environment flags and errno are not exposed by this Go API.
